ok 1 - TWO RUNS STARTED TOGETHER: the second WAITS, names the first's seat, pid and command, and runs only after it
ok 2 - A STALE LOCK (its pid is dead) is taken over, and the takeover is logged with the holder and its age
ok 3 - a LIVE holder is never taken over: after the max wait the second FAILS LOUDLY with the holder's details and does not run
ok 4 - RELEASE ON A THROWN ERROR: a runner that throws leaves no lock behind
ok 5 - RELEASE ON SIGINT: the handler hold() installs releases and exits 130 (the handler, run by emitting the signal in-process)
ok 6 - RELEASE ON NORMAL EXIT, and release removes only its OWN lock
ok 7 - a NESTED run under the holder (its token in the environment) is the same run: it does not wait and does not release
ok 8 - a token that is NOT the current holder's (a child of some earlier run) is no pass: it waits like anyone else
ok 9 - no data dir is a REFUSAL, never a run without the lock
ok 10 - the lock holds {pid, seat, cmd, started} (and the token, since D286 the tree, and since L124 the holder's identity {image, holder_start})
ok 11 - pidAlive: this process is alive; a pid that does not exist is not
ok 12 - D283 (RED FIRST) the claimed false takeover: kill(0) reads a 5-minute-old holder dead, tasklist reads it RUNNING: the lock is NOT taken, the disagreement is said once with both readings, and at the max wait it fails loudly
