ok 14 - D283 a young lock the second method CANNOT judge (null) is not taken: unknown is the safe side; it waits and fails loudly
ok 15 - D283 an OLD lock (30 minutes or more) is taken on kill(0) alone: the second method is never asked; to the millisecond
ok 16 - D283 a lock whose age cannot be read (no started, or junk) counts as YOUNG: the second witness is asked
ok 17 - D283 PID REUSE fails safe: a lock whose pid is now some OTHER live process reads alive on every method, so the waiter waits and gives up loudly (real methods)
