ok 19 - D283 REAL: a holder killed HARD (as a stopped task is) leaves its lock, and the next runner takes it over at once, logged, naming the dead pid (real kill(0) and real tasklist)
ok 20 - D283 pidGone: tasklist is asked for exactly that pid; a listed row means running; no row (exit 0) means gone; a failure, an error or garbage means "cannot tell"; off Windows kill(0) is the whole truth
ok 21 - D289 pidGone: a call that timed out after tasklist exited 0 (error set, status 0, partial output) is "cannot tell", not gone
ok 22 - D283 pidAlive: EPERM is alive (not allowed to touch it is not dead); ESRCH, any other error and a bad pid are not
ok 23 - D283 a race: a LIVE lock created between the read and the takeover is put back, not clobbered, and the waiter keeps waiting
ok 24 - D289 a race: a YOUNG lock caught by the rename is not thrown away on kill(0) alone; it is put back, tasklist is asked, and while tasklist says RUNNING the waiter waits
